    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a2">

                <pb facs="0277" n="221" xml:id="pg221"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in inclosure in No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">Tuesday</hi>, 28<hi
                                rendition="#italic">th</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Daily News, March 29.]</p>
                <p>The United States district court of New York has decided that the forger
                    Lawrence, who was brought from England under the extradition treaty, can be
                    tried for other offenses besides those mentioned in the warrant. The court
                    cannot regard the order of the President to the contrary, or take notice of any
                    agreement between the English and American governments to that effect.</p>
            </div>
